== Data Ingestion, Extraction, and Schema Translation

To bridge live Windows domain controllers and our PyTorch Geometric deep learning pipeline, we engineered an automated data ingestion and schema translation engine implemented in `bloodhound_parser.py`.

=== Active Directory Telemetry Collection

Data collection against the live GOAD virtual machines was conducted using the SharpHound v5 collector executed from unprivileged domain accounts. SharpHound queries the Active Directory Global Catalog via LDAP (TCP 389/636), Active Directory Web Services (TCP 9389), and NetBIOS/SMB (TCP 445), extracting:

+ Security Principal metadata (Users, Computers, Groups, CAs, Templates).
+ Group membership nesting hierarchies (`MemberOf`).
+ Active user logon sessions via NetSessionEnum and Remote Registry APIs.
+ Full Discretionary Access Control Lists (DACLs) from directory security descriptors.
+ Certificate template attributes and Enterprise CA enrollment publication lists.



=== Graph Schema Translation Pipeline

The raw JSON data structures generated by SharpHound were ingested and converted into PyTorch Geometric `HeteroData` tensors via a four-stage translation process:

+ *Identity and SID Disambiguation:* Windows Security Identifiers (e.g., `S-1-5-21-123456789-500`) and Distinguished Names (DNs) are mapped to contiguous 0-indexed integer identifiers within disjoint typed node partitions ($V_("User")$, $V_("Computer")$, $V_("Group")$, $V_("Template")$, $V_("CA")$).
+ *Attribute Vectorization:* LDAP property dictionaries are parsed to extract binary feature vectors. Certificate template flags (`msPKI-Certificate-Name-Flag`, `pKIExtendedKeyUsage`, `msPKI-Certificate-Policy`) are converted into the 10-dimensional template feature vector $x_("Template") in bb(R)^(10)$.
+ *Relational Edge Mapping:* Active Directory Access Control Entries (ACEs) and enrollment permissions are categorized into canonical directed relation tensors ($E_("MemberOf")$, $E_("Enroll")$, $E_("GenericAll")$, $E_("WriteDacl")$, $E_("WriteOwner")$, $E_("PublishedTo")$, $E_("ManageCA")$, $E_("LinksPolicy")$).
+ *Reverse Canonical Relation Generation:* For every extracted directed edge tensor $E_r$, the transposed edge tensor $E_(r^(-1)) = {(v, r^(-1), u) | (u, r, v) in E_r}$ is generated to facilitate bidirectional relational message passing.



