As shown in @tab:community_results, across 30 test scenarios spanning the three external enterprise domains, CertGraph-Hybrid maintained *100.0% accuracy* (30/30, Wilson CI: $[0.886, 1.000]$), pure CertGraph achieved *80.0%* (misclassifying the 2 hard negative templates in each domain), and signature-based Certipy heuristics achieved only *63.3%*. The performance gain of $+36.7%$ over Certipy stems from the dual advantage of relational discovery (ESC13) and symbolic false-positive suppression on hard negative templates. This confirms that our findings replicate cleanly on independent directory collections.
